  "folder": "k5SXmlVACc2CKVy0",
  "sort": 0,
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>Highlord Darion Mograine turned Shadow's Edge into Shadowmourne once the axe had been infused with unholy power, blood magic, and undying frost, along with shadowfrost shards from the Frozen Throne.</p><p><strong>Magic Weapon.</strong> You gain a +3 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with this weapon.</p><p><strong>Soul Fragments.</strong> When you hit a creature with a melee attack roll using Shadowmourne, it takes an extra 1d12 Necrotic damage, and you gain Temporary Hit Points equal to the Necrotic damage it takes.</p><p><strong>Drain Soul.</strong> Whenever you use Shadowmourne to reduce a creature to 0 Hit Points, the axe slays it and devours its soul unless it is a Construct. Only a Wish spell can restore to life a creature whose soul was devoured. When Shadowmourne devours a soul, you gain Temporary Hit Points equal to the slain creature's Hit Point maximum.</p><p><strong>Chaos Bane.</strong> If you have at least 12 Temporary Hit Points, you can take a Bonus Action to sacrifice all of them. Each creature of your choice in a 15-foot Emanation originating from you makes a DC 21 Constitution saving throw, taking damage equal to the Temporary Hit Points sacrificed on a failure or half as much on a success. Until the end of your next turn, you have Advantage on attack rolls and saving throws.</p><p><strong>Random Properties.</strong> This Artifact has the following random properties (see <em>Artifact Traits</em> in the module journal): 2 minor beneficial properties, 2 major beneficial properties, 2 minor detrimental properties, 2 major detrimental properties.</p><p><strong>Destroying the Weapon.</strong> The axe is destroyed if immersed in a pool of fresh blood of an Old God, which frees the souls it devoured.</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-evWWvhz8zFC5BWjH\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p>Soul Fragments: enter the Necrotic damage rolled as Temporary Hit Points. Chaos Bane deals damage equal to the Temporary Hit Points you sacrifice (set them to 0 afterward).</p></section>",
      "chat": ""
    },
